    <section class="tx-shell tx-faq" id="TxFaq-{{ section.id }}">
      <div class="tx-section-heading"><span>Before you decide</span><h2>Common questions about color correction</h2></div>
      <details open><summary>Will these permanently whiten my teeth?</summary><p>No. They are color-correcting oral-care tablets, not a permanent bleaching treatment. Purple pigment is intended to help temporarily reduce the appearance of warm yellow tones after brushing.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How are they different from whitening strips?</summary><p>Whitening strips commonly use peroxide to create a deeper shade change over a treatment cycle. Trainixy tablets are peroxide-free and use a color-correcting approach in a simple chew-and-brush format.</p></details>
      <details><summary>How do I use a tablet?</summary><p>Chew one tablet until it forms a fine foam, brush gently as directed for 2–3 minutes, then spit and rinse thoroughly. Do not swallow.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can results look different from person to person?</summary><p>Yes. The visible effect can vary with your natural tooth shade, the cause and degree of discoloration, lighting and how regularly you use the product.</p></details>
      <details><summary>What if I have crowns, veneers or ongoing sensitivity?</summary><p>Dental restorations may respond differently from natural teeth. Ask your dentist before use if you have visible restorations, active dental concerns or persistent sensitivity.</p></details>
    </section>

